[{"category":"section","location":"#Penalized-splines","page":"Penalized splines","text":"Fit two spline models to the same simulated EEG and compare their predicted event-related responses. Both models use the same spline basis. The second estimates the smoothing strengths with REML.","title":"Penalized splines"},{"category":"section","location":"#Load-the-example-data","page":"Penalized splines","text":"Run the example from the package repository. UnfoldSim generated the recording from 200 events. Both predictors affect the height of the P300 peak. Simulation code and data\n\n<details><summary>Setup</summary>\n\njulia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'\njulia --project=assets -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'\n\nStart Julia with julia --project=. and load the saved recording.\n\nusing Unfold, UnfoldPenalizedSplines, DataFrames, DelimitedFiles\n\nfolder = \"results/erp_effects\"\nevent_rows, _ = readdlm(joinpath(folder, \"events.csv\"), ',', Float64; header=true)\nrecording, _ = readdlm(joinpath(folder, \"recording.csv\"), ',', Float64; header=true)\nevents = DataFrame(x1=event_rows[:, 1], x2=event_rows[:, 2],\n                   latency=Int.(event_rows[:, 3]))\ndata = reshape(recording[:, 3], 1, :)\n\n</details>","title":"Load the example data"},{"category":"section","location":"#Fit-the-spline-models","page":"Penalized splines","text":"Use the same formula and time window for both fits.\n\nformula = @formula(0 ~ 1 + pspl(x1, 8) + pspl(x2, 8))\nbasis = firbasis(τ=(-0.1, 0.5), sfreq=100; interpolate=false)\n\nunpenalized = fit(UnfoldModel, formula, events, data, basis)\npenalized = fit_pspl(formula, events, data, basis)","title":"Fit the spline models"},{"category":"section","location":"#Plot-the-marginal-effects","page":"Penalized splines","text":"Use effects() to predict the response at 21 values of x₁ with x₂ held at zero. Each color represents one x₁ value.\n\ngrid = Dict(:x1 => -2:0.2:2, :x2 => [0.0])\neffects_unpenalized = effects(grid, unpenalized)\neffects_penalized = effects(grid, penalized)\n\n(Image: Predicted EEG responses across x₁ for the unpenalized and REML-smoothed fits)\n\nThe left panel uses zero penalties. In the right panel, REML estimates λ₁ ≈ 0.6430 and λ₂ ≈ 69.82. The penalties control how much the response can bend across predictor values.\n\nRun julia --project=. examples/erp_effects.jl to regenerate the figure. Example code · Plot code","title":"Plot the marginal effects"},{"category":"section","location":"#Adjust-spline-smoothing","page":"Penalized splines","text":"Move either slider to see the predictions from a fit with those two smoothing strengths. Both sliders start at the REML estimates. The left plot varies x₁ at x₂ = 0, and the right plot varies x₂ at x₁ = 0.\n\n<iframe id=\"spline-smoothing-demo\" src=\"assets/smoothing-demo.htm?v=two-sliders\" title=\"Adjust the smoothing strengths of the x1 and x2 splines\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display: block; width: 100%; height: 720px; border: 0; background: white; color-scheme: only light;\"></iframe>\n<script src=\"assets/embed-demo.js\"></script>\n\nDemo fitting · Demo plots","title":"Adjust spline smoothing"}]
